<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32185" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκ-κλητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽἐκκαλέὠ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>selected to judge</i> or
				<i>arbitrate</i> on a point, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ.
			πόλις</span> an <i>umpire</i> city, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.89
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.111.49
			</span></i>,al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.215c
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἐκκλήτῳ δικάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Michel</u>
					1335.30
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκην ὠφληκὼς ἐν τῇ ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(7).67.63
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρόνος ἔ.</span> time-limit <i>for appeals,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PRev.Laws
				21.15
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἔκκλητοι,</span> in Sparta and
			elsewhere, <i>a committee of citizens chosen to report</i> on
			certain questions, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.4.38
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. Ἀργείων ὄχλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					612
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				949
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>subject to appeal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.111.74
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				52.22
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHal.</u>
					1.68
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς
			ἐκκλήτους</span> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκας</span>]..<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ αὑτὸν
				ποιούμενος,</span> prob. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγκ-,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				1348b14
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκκλητον δικάζειν</span>
			exercise <i>appellate</i> jurisdiction, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				51.19
			</span></i>.</div>
